{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"alias":"moist-short-lionfish","creation_channel":"cli","description":"## Context / Problem\nEvery rebar ticket write on a real store logs\n`WARNING rebar.llm.enrich_drain: enrich drain gate check took 500-740 ms (> 20 ms budget)`.\nObserved on EVERY write in a 2026-08-19 session against this repo's own tracker.\n\nMeasured (worktree of origin/main at 09947b1, warm page cache, 4710 ticket dirs in\n`.tickets-tracker`):\n\n    Q.pending_enrichment(...) x3 -> 797.9 ms, 743.5 ms, 724.6 ms   (pending=0 each time)\n    Q.reduce_ticket x300         -> 38.5 ms  (~0.128 ms/ticket)\n\n0.128 ms/ticket x 4710 = ~600 ms, which accounts for the whole figure. So this is NOT a cold\n-path/first-run cost (it repeats warm, run after run) and NOT a recent regression: the gate is\nLINEAR in the number of ticket directories, and `maybe_drain`'s 20 ms budget\n(`overlap_drain_gate_budget_ms`) is only reachable at roughly <=150 tickets. The store crossed\nthat threshold long ago.\n\n`maybe_drain`'s docstring calls this a \"cheap 'is anything soaked?' check that no-ops in the\ncommon case\". It is not cheap: `overlap.queue.pending_enrichment` lists the tracker and calls\n`reduce_ticket` for EVERY ticket dir, each of which scans that ticket's events three times\n(`_latest` for ENQUEUE / CLAIM / DONE). The common case — nothing soaked — costs a full store\nwalk.\n\nTwo distinct harms:\n1. **Latency on the write path.** `maybe_drain` runs opportunistically on ordinary\n   invocations whenever `verify.suggest_duplicate_tickets` is on, so every ticket write pays\n   ~0.6-0.8 s of pure overhead before returning.\n2. **A dead observability signal.** The budget breach is designed to be a warning an operator\n   acts on. Firing on 100% of writes makes it noise, so a genuine future breach is invisible.\n\n## Approach (to be confirmed by whoever claims this)\nNot yet decided; the point of this ticket is to pick one deliberately rather than let the\nwarning keep firing. Candidate directions, cheapest first:\n- Make the gate O(1)-ish instead of O(tickets) — e.g. a queue-head/soonest-`not_before_ns`\n  marker under `.rebar` maintained by `enqueue`/`mark_done`, so the common \"nothing soaked\"\n  answer needs one read rather than a full store walk. Must stay self-healing (a lost or\n  stale marker degrades to the current scan, never to a missed drain).\n- Or recalibrate/scale `overlap_drain_gate_budget_ms` with store size, and downgrade the\n  repeat-warning to a once-per-process log, so the signal stays meaningful.\nBoth must keep the drain's existing no-op-on-Windows / never-raise contract.\n\n## Scope\n- `src/rebar/llm/enrich_drain.py` (the gate + its budget warning)\n- `src/rebar/llm/overlap/queue.py` (`pending_enrichment`, and any marker written by\n  `enqueue` / `mark_done`)\n- corresponding tests under `tests/unit/`\n\n## Testing\n- A test that plants N enqueued tickets and asserts the gate's work does not grow linearly\n  with N (e.g. counts `reduce_ticket` calls, rather than asserting a wall-clock number, so it\n  is not flaky on a loaded CI runner).\n- A test that a lost/corrupt marker still finds a genuinely soaked ticket (self-healing).\n- A test that the budget warning does not fire once per write on a large store.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n- [ ] The gate's cost on a store with no soaked entries is independent of the ticket count,\n      asserted by a call-count test rather than a wall-clock assertion.\n- [ ] A soaked ticket is still found after the fast path's marker is deleted or corrupted.\n- [ ] The budget-breach WARNING no longer fires on an ordinary write against a store of\n      several thousand tickets.\n- [ ] `make lint`, `make typecheck` and CI's pytest invocation are green.\n\n## Provenance\nDiscovered while implementing task deathful-lettered-maltesedog (8d78-ef59-83cd-4d76); out of\nthat ticket's scope, filed rather than fixed there.","id":"958e-f4b3-275c-4154","parent_id":"","priority":2,"tags":[],"ticket_type":"bug","title":"enrich drain gate check is O(ticket count), blowing its 20 ms budget on every write"},"env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","event_type":"CREATE","timestamp":1787175326523995001,"uuid":"f751387f-323a-4788-9fb2-e95c569cfe8b"}